        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Gigapixel upscale\n\nUpscales any image to about **1.67 gigapixels** (the pixel budget of a 4 x 3 m poster at 300 DPI). The aspect ratio of the source is kept, nothing is cropped.\n\n## How it works\n1. **Stage 1 size** fits the source into an 8192 x 8192 box (aspect kept).\n2. Two upscalers bring it there: **Nomos2** 4x (faithful, clean) and **SeedVR2 7B** (diffusion, adds real texture).\n3. **Frequency blend**: tones and shapes from Nomos2, fine texture from a 25/75 Nomos2/SeedVR2 mix.\n4. **Poster scale** resizes the 8192 px master to the final size with plain Lanczos. A second AI pass here only turns grain into fake scratches, so it is a plain resize on purpose.\n\n## Camera photo switch (orange)\n- **false** (default): AI renders and clean, sharp photos, studio product shots included. Uses the blend.\n- **true**: only soft or noisy camera shots (phone, high ISO, missed focus). Uses RealESRGAN, skips Nomos2 and SeedVR2.\n- If unsure, leave it false.\n\nMeasured on 150 images with ground truth: the blend wins on AI renders and clean photos, RealESRGAN wins on real camera photos.\n\n## Poster scale\nSet it for the aspect of your source to land at about 1.67 GP:\n\n| Source aspect | Master | Poster scale | Poster |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1:1 | 8192 x 8192 | 4.99 | ~40,880 x 40,880 |\n| 4:3 | 8192 x 6144 | 5.77 | ~47,270 x 35,450 |\n| 3:2 | 8192 x 5464 | 6.11 | ~50,050 x 33,380 |\n| 16:9 | 8192 x 4608 | 6.65 | ~54,480 x 30,640 |\n\n## Source\n- At least **2048 px on the long side**. Below that SeedVR2 goes past 4x and starts inventing material.\n- Check fine print (packaging text) at 100 percent: small text is where every upscaler fails first.\n\n## Outputs\n- **gigapixel/master**: the 8192 px master. Review this one.\n- **gigapixel/poster**: the full-size PNG. ComfyUI writes no DPI tag: in Photoshop use Image Size with Resample off, set 300 DPI, then save as PSB or TIFF (PSD stops at 30,000 px).\n- On a remote pod the poster PNG is slow to write and to download. Downloading only the master and resizing locally is faster.\n\n## Requirements\n- ComfyUI 0.28.0 or newer (tested on 0.30.0), ComfyUI-KJNodes (tested on 1.5.0).\n- About 40 GB of VRAM at 4:3, more at 1:1. Roughly 45 GB of free RAM for the poster step.\n- Time on an RTX PRO 6000: about 2 to 4 minutes for the master, then a few minutes for the poster PNG.\n- All four models are needed even if you only use the camera switch.\n\n## Models\n```\nComfyUI/models/\n  upscale_models/4xNomos2_hq_dat2.safetensors    huggingface.co/Phips/4xNomos2_hq_dat2 (CC BY 4.0, Philip Hofmann)\n  upscale_models/RealESRGAN_x4plus.pth           github.com/xinntao/Real-ESRGAN releases v0.1.0\n  diffusion_models/seedvr2_7b_int8_convrot.safetensors   huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/SeedVR2\n  vae/seedvr2_ema_vae_fp16.safetensors           huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/SeedVR2\n```\n"
      ],
      "title": "Read me"
    }
